# Trivy suppressions for aws-edge-security-platform.
#
# Only findings that cannot be fixed without breaking the design are listed, and
# each one carries the reason. Everything else is expected to pass.

# AVD-AWS-0057 - IAM policy should avoid wildcards.
# modules/waf-logs/firehose.tf grants logs:PutLogEvents on
# "${aws_cloudwatch_log_group.firehose.arn}:*". A CloudWatch Logs group ARN must
# carry a ":*" suffix to reach the log streams inside it - that is the form AWS
# documents, and without it the delivery stream cannot report its own errors.
# Every other statement in that policy names an explicit ARN.
AVD-AWS-0057

# AVD-AWS-0010 - CloudFront distribution should have access logging.
# Standard logging is wired up in modules/cloudfront/main.tf, but through a
# dynamic block that only activates when the caller passes
# var.log_bucket_domain_name. Trivy reads the static configuration and cannot see
# it. The waf-logs module also ships real-time logs via Kinesis Data Streams and
# Firehose, which is what the security analytics in this repo actually query.
AVD-AWS-0010
